4
00:00:17,628 --> 00:00:20,235
What is a G L M?

5
00:00:20,235 --> 00:00:29,363
The general linear model represents the measured bold time series as a weighted combination of explanatory variables plus unexplained residual error.

6
00:00:29,363 --> 00:00:35,013
FEAT fits this model separately at each voxel while accounting for temporal structure.

7
00:00:35,013 --> 00:00:42,402
The design matrix contains one row per time point and columns for task predictors and nuisance regressors.

8
00:00:42,402 --> 00:00:45,010
Parameter estimates describe each column's contribution.

9
00:00:45,010 --> 00:00:51,530
A good-looking activation map cannot rescue a design matrix that does not represent the experiment.

10
00:00:52,380 --> 00:00:56,152
